  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n[(15% of A) × (35% of B)] ÷ 21% of C = 37\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nAccording to the question,\n\n(frac{15A)/(100)×(35B)/(100)}{(21C)/(100)} = 37\n\n⇒ {(15A)/(100)×(35B)/(100)}×{(100)/(21C)} = 37\n\n⇒ {(AB)/(4C)} = 37\n\nSo,\n\n{(AB)/(C)} = 37 × 4\n\n⇒ {(AB)/(C)} = 148\n\n**∴ Required answer is 148.**\n\n2d4",
